wmime 1.2.0 (2026-10-27)
========================

* Removed extraneous `const` qualifiers on return types that prevented
  feeding generate() return values to another function as movable rvalues.
* Over-encoding ASCII words in RFC 6532 mode is avoided.
* The Date: line parser is now in line with RFC 5322, abolishing
  recognition for single-letter time zones previously availablein RFC 822.
* Added support for IMAP ID extension.
* Added support for Cygwin.
* Header folding is now in accordance with RFC 5322/2047.
* In e.g. To: address lists, '(' and '<' were erroneously parsed as comment and
  start of address even when they appeared in a quoted display name, which has
  been fixed.


wmime 1.1.0 (2025-07-21)
========================

* Original MIME boundary are now preserved when parsing and regenerating
  messages.
* Made generateRandomBytes() not produce undefined bytes.


wmime 1.0.0
===========

* Improved address parser for malformed mailbox specifications.
* Whitespace between leading boundary hyphens and marker is now ignored.
* Display names that are representable as-is are no longer forcibly
  qp/b64-encoded.
* When sending over sendmail:// transport, the MAIL FROM envelope
  address is no longer emitted as zero-length garbage.
* Added support for IPv6 literals to vmime::url.
* Cured bad outcomes from `wordEncoder::guessBestEncoding` for input
  longer than 42.94 MB.
* Added/updated support for FreeBSD libc++ and Solaris systems.
* Space characters are no longer lost during text::createFromString.
